{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall make atonement for her.</b> One may explain it in the sense of cleansing, like that case of ״he wiped his hands with his fellow's garment,״ and likewise ״and he shall make atonement for him who is to be cleansed״ in the case of the metzora, and likewise ״and he shall make atonement for the house״ in the case of nega'im, and likewise ״and he shall make atonement for him״ in the case of the zav. In all of these it is not actual atonement for sin that applies, for even though nega'im come on account of transgressions, nevertheless there is atonement in nega'im and in the yoledet. Even though our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said that she sins at the moment she crouches to give birth — she vows that she will not have relations with her husband again — nevertheless according to the plain sense of the verse it does not imply that her offering comes on account of sin, and וכפר means nothing but cleansing, like ״and you shall purify the house.״"], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:31.713111364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}